<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafting-professions">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Professions &amp; Crafted Gear for Retribution Paladin</span></h2>Every profession is viable in Mists of Pandaria, though the best two professions in Phase 3 are <b>Engineering</b> combined with either <b>Tailoring</b>, <b>Herbalism</b> or <b>Blacksmithing</b> which all perform within 1% of each other, so they are all respectable choices.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="engineering">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_engineering.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Engineering for Retribution Paladin</h4>Engineering is typically incredibly powerful in World of Warcraft and Mists of Pandaria is no different. The main reason to be an Engineer is to utilize the glove enchant <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=126731/synapse-springs">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Synapse Springs</span></a> which will provide us with +1920 strength for 10 seconds every minute, a potent cooldown when overlapped with your other cooldowns. <br/>
<br/>Engineering also makes it possible to use explosives like <a class="q1 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=42641/global-thermal-sapper-charge">
<img alt="Global Thermal Sapper Charge" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gizmo_supersappercharge.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Global Thermal Sapper Charge</span></a>, however many of them are either weak at this point, or not instant-cast, so they are not actually used by that many people anymore in PvE raid content. The only somewhat relevant explosive, <a class="q1 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77589/g91-landshark">
<img alt="G91 Landshark" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_landshark.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">G91 Landshark</span></a> which is very useful in Challenge Modes, does not require Engineering. <br/>
<br/>Engineering also provides access to <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77539/reinforced-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Reinforced Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reinforced Retinal Armor</span></a> which is a powerful early item, particularly for Challenge Modes.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="blacksmithing">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_blacksmithing.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Blacksmithing for Retribution Paladin</h4>Blacksmithing does allow you to craft some Epic plate DPS gear, but all of these items are Bind-on-Equip and can be purchased from the Auction House or crafted by someone else and then traded to you. <br/>
<br/>Instead, the main benefit of being a Blacksmith is the extra gem slots provided by <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=114112/socket-gloves">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_addsocketglove.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Socket Gloves</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=113263/socket-bracer">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/item_socketedbracer.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Socket Bracer</span></a>. This makes the benefit of Blacksmithing rather flexible, as these gem slots can provide anywhere from +640 Haste to +320 Strength to +640 Hit if you really badly need more Hit chance. Likewise, you can mix and match gems and use hybrid color gems in order to dial in exactly what you need most. That being said, most of the time you will want the +640 Haste from having two extra <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76699/quick-suns-radiance">
<img alt="Quick Sun's Radiance" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_yellow.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Quick Sun's Radiance</span></a> gems.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="tailoring">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_tailoring.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Tailoring for Retribution Paladin</h4>While we have no use for any of the cloth items that can be crafted with Tailoring, the cloak enchant <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=125483/swordguard-embroidery">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_thread_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Swordguard Embroidery</span></a> is actually quite powerful, as the +4000 Attack Power proc on a 1-minute cooldown can often stack neatly with our cooldowns.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="herbalism">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_herbalism.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Herbalism for Retribution Paladin</h4>Herbalism is not only a great money-making profession, it also provides us with the cooldown <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=121279/lifeblood">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_wispsplodegreen.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lifeblood</span></a> granting +2880 Haste for 20 seconds, once every 2-minutes. Haste is one of our best stats, and this is easily stacked with <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=31884/avenging-wrath">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_avenginewrath.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Avenging Wrath</span></a>, which makes it rather potent.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Crafted Gear for Retribution Paladin</span></h3>Crafted items are, for the most part, bind-on-equip - meaning you don't need to be any specific profession in order to gain access to them. One exception to this rule is the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77539/reinforced-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Reinforced Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reinforced Retinal Armor</span></a> which requires Engineering.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94266/haunted-steel-greathelm">
<img alt="Haunted Steel Greathelm" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_plate_raidwarrior_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Haunted Steel Greathelm</span></a> - a 522 item level helmet that is craftable with the new reagents available in Phase 3, and in a vacuum will be better than anything available outside of raid.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94267/haunted-steel-warboots">
<img alt="Haunted Steel Warboots" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_plate_deathknight_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Haunted Steel Warboots</span></a> - a 522 item level pair of boots that is craftable with the new reagents available in Phase 3, and in a vacuum will be better than anything available outside of raid.<br/>
<span class="small-text">If you need the hit, then choose these over the Treads.</span></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94265/haunted-steel-treads">
<img alt="Haunted Steel Treads" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_plate_raidwarrior_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Haunted Steel Treads</span></a> - a 522 item level pair of boots that is craftable with the new reagents available in Phase 3, and in a vacuum will be better than anything available outside of raid.<br/>
<span class="small-text">If you don't need the hit, then choose these over the Warboots.</span></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77539/reinforced-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Reinforced Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reinforced Retinal Armor</span></a> - the only bind-on-pickup crafted item, which requires Engineering, and is one of the more potent crafted items available; especially notable when you first reach max level. Due to the powerful cogwheel gems that can be slotted in, it is a popular choice for Challenge Mode content where gems avoid the downward scaling.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87407/bloodforged-warfists">
<img alt="Bloodforged Warfists" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlet_plate_raidwarrior_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bloodforged Warfists</span></a> - high item-level gloves crafted by Blacksmiths with a recipe obtained inside of raids, outclassed only by raid items.</div></li>
